<title>SINGAPORE: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>SINGAPORE GOVERNMENT LIST (961223)</p>
<p>   ***********************************************************</p>
<p>   * 23 Dec 96 - General elections are to take place on	*</p>
<p>   *		 January 2. Prime minister Goh has already   *</p>
<p>   *		 claimed victory for the PAP, since the	*</p>
<p>   *		 opposition will only contest 36 of the 83   *</p>
<p>   *		 seats in parliament, assuring the PAP of a  *</p>
<p>   *		 majority.					     *</p>
<p>   ***********************************************************</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p>  President (Sworn in 1 Sep 93).................ONG Teng Cheong</p>
<p>  Presidential Adviser..............................LIM Kim San</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p>PEOPLE'S ACTION PARTY GOVERNMENT (Formed 5 Sept 91,</p>
<p>	    Reshuffle announced June 28, effective Aug 1 1995)</p>
<p>  Prime Minister..................................GOH Chok Tong</p>
<p>  Senior Minister (Prime Minister's Office)........LEE Kuan Yew</p>
<p>  Deputy Prime Minister.........................LEE Hsien Loong</p>
<p>  Deputy Prime Minister................................Tony TAN</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Defence)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>  Communications....................................MAH Bow Tan</p>
<p>  Community Development........................Abdullah TARMUGI</p>
<p>  Defence........................................See Deputy PMs</p>
<p>  Education.......................................LEE Yock Suan</p>
<p>  Environment.....................................TEO Chee Hean</p>
<p>Finance, National Development, Chairman of the Monetary</p>
<p>	Authority of Singapore (MAS)...................Richard HU</p>
<p>  Foreign Affairs, Law......................Shanmugam JAYAKUMAR</p>
<p>  Home Affairs....................................WONG Kan Seng</p>
<p>  Information &amp; the Arts, Health.....................George YEO</p>
<p>  Labour..........................................LEE Boon Yang</p>
<p>  National Development............................LIM Hng Kiang</p>
<p>  Trade and Industry.............................YEO Cheow Tong</p>
<p>  Without Portfolio...............................LIM Boon Heng</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Chairman of the Monetary Authority</p>
<p>     of Singapore (MAS)....................See Finance Minister</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			(End Government List)</p>
</text>
